{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjWbpFPRM1w7G2Zojo5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about what happens when a token expires mid-batch in this code. Let me analyze the code:\n\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    for item in page.items:\n        client.push(item, token=token)   # raises AuthExpired\n    checkpoint(page.id)\n```\n\nThe issue here is about where processing resumes if `AuthExpired` is raised.\n\nLooking at the logic:\n1. For each page, it iterates through all items\n2. If `AuthExpired` is raised on any item, the exception will propagate up (it's not caught)\n3. The `checkpoint(page.id)` is only called after ALL items in a page are successfully pushed\n4. When execution resumes (after getting a new token), the outer loop will continue from where it left off - the `for page in pages` will pick up from the next page (not the current one)\n\nSo if an `AuthExpired` exception occurs:\n- It will resume from the NEXT page\n- It will restart the failed page from the beginning (re-processing all its items)\n- Any items that were successfully pushed before the failure will be pushed again (assuming they're idempotent, or might create duplicates if they're not)\n\nThe current design has the checkpoint at the page level, so it only commits progress after the entire page is done. This means:\n- If token expires on item 5 of page 1 (which has 100 items)\n- On retry, it will restart page 1 from item 1 (all 100 items)\n- Items 1-4 will be re-pushed (idempotency issue if the service doesn't handle duplicates)\n\nThe user is asking where it leaves off - they want to know if it resumes from the failed item or restarts the page. The answer is: it restarts the page.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6948,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6948},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"75e1a857-c6b8-4f7e-aad8-6ce030a0ef83","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:40:41.691Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjWZrgCGxMQ7BYrYXf5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjWbpFPRM1w7G2Zojo5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It **restarts the page** from the beginning.\n\nThe `checkpoint(page.id)` only fires after *all* items in a page succeed. When `AuthExpired` is raised mid-page, the exception propagates, no checkpoint is saved, and the outer loop is suspended. On retry (after refreshing the token), `for page in pages` resumes from the *next* page—but the failed page never checkpointed, so it starts over.\n\n**Problem:** Items 1–4 get pushed twice (duplicate risk if not idempotent).\n\n**To resume from the failed item**, checkpoint at the item level instead:\n\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    for item in page.items:\n        client.push(item, token=token)   # raises AuthExpired\n        checkpoint(page.id, item.id)     # save progress per-item\n```\n\nOr store state more explicitly:\n\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    for idx, item in enumerate(page.items):\n        if checkpoint_read((page.id, idx)) is not None:\n            continue  # skip already-pushed\n        client.push(item, token=token)\n        checkpoint_write((page.id, idx))\n```\n\nThe trade-off: per-item checkpoints are slower but survive mid-page failures; per-page checkpoints are faster but force replays."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6948,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6948},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"e0ef9c49-d57c-4972-8841-1986de5493f0","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:40:45.012Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjWZrgCGxMQ7BYrYXf5"}
